<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patria Boba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1810–1816</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Foolish Fatherland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patria Boba, the 'Foolish Fatherland', is the name given to the first period of independence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>, present-day Colombia, from 1810 to 1816. Federalists of the United Provinces and centralists of Cundinamarca fought each other in civil wars instead of uniting against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The period ended when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pablo-morillo">Pablo Morillo</a>'s expedition reconquered the country and executed many patriot leaders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patria-boba.jpg" alt="Patria Boba" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Racso · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Granada_(1811-1814).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
